okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: cli runtime이 스스로 재시작을 위한 기능을 만들지 않았어? mcp에 노출 안 했어? / 로컬에 배포했어? 이 muse가 못찾는데 - make a Muse Code session able to use the router's MCP tools (restart_session) and apply it locally."
finding:
  feature_exists: "The restart feature is c53d12e: a request file the owning launcher polls, then the CLI is terminated and relaunched with its session-continue argument (claude --continue, codex resume --last, muse resume). The MCP tool restart_session is declared in channel_mcp_tools.py and served by the workspace router at /ca/mcp."
  why_muse_missed_it: "Muse launches never attached the router MCP server: router_mcp_enabled_for_launch() is applied in runtime_launch.py for Claude (:501) and Codex (:991) only, and muse_runtime_context.py had no MCP code at all. Muse also has no --mcp-config flag - it reads `mcpServers` from ~/.config/muse/settings.json (inside WSL on Windows)."
  why_the_cli_missed_it: "The shell in WSL resolved ciel-runtime/ciel-runtimectl from the npm global install, which was 0.2.47-nightly.20260917 (before the restart feature). The menu, statusline, presence and stop helpers never carried subcommands."
built:
  muse_mcp.py: "Merges one `ciel-runtime-router` entry {type streamable-http, url <router>/ca/mcp, Authorization Bearer <token>, mode optional} into Muse's settings.json, preserving every other key and server; removes the entry when a launch has no managed router; never overwrites an unreadable file. IO goes through a callable so the same code drives a native file or `wsl -e sh -lc` for the Windows/WSL boundary."
  policy: "router_mcp_decision(): loopback router -> local placeholder token; Muse in WSL + loopback router -> skip and log the remedy (`--ca-web-address <windows-wsl-ip>`); non-loopback without the external token -> skip and name the flag. muse.router_mcp=false disables the attach."
  wiring: "muse_runtime_context.launch() syncs the entry for interactive sessions (attach when a router is managed, remove otherwise); MuseLifecyclePorts gained a log port, wired to router_log on the existing endpoint line (ciel_runtime.py stays at its 4,980-line budget)."
verification:
  tests: "tests/test_muse_mcp.py (15) - entry shape, decision policy per platform/bind, merge refresh and removal, unreadable-file refusal, native round-trip, WSL bridge argv+payload; tests/test_muse_runtime.py +5 - attach entry for a native launch, skip with the WSLL reason over loopback, attach with the external token for a reachable host, muse.router_mcp=false, utility commands untouched. unit 1556 OK, router 1139 OK, runtime 296 OK, ruff clean."
  wsl_reachability: "A router started with CIEL_RUNTIME_ROUTER_BIND_HOST=172.29.112.1 and external access served /ca/mcp, and `curl` from WSL with the external token returned tools/list including restart_session. A plain listener on the same address also answered 200 from WSL, so the Windows firewall permits it."
  real_settings_file: "Merged the entry into the user's actual ~/.config/muse/settings.json through the WSL bridge: attach produced servers [ciel-runtime-router, walkie_http] with model/provider untouched, removal restored the file byte-for-byte (json-equal to a pre-test backup). Backup kept at .tmp/muse-settings-backup-20260919.json."
  live_router_tools: "tools/list on the running routers: 9465 (new build) and 9491 (F:\aap.ezonebot, new build) include restart_session; 9611 (this Claude session, snapshot 984e05f) does not - the feature predates that build."
applied_to_the_machine:
  npm_global: "npm i -g @oneciel-ai/ciel-runtime@nightly (Windows npm prefix %APPDATA%\npm, the one WSL sees through /mnt/c) -> 0.2.51-nightly.20260919-070852.c3a76f4; `ciel-runtimectl restart-session --help` now answers in WSL."
  workspace: "workspaces/08c021f4fb95 (F:\aap.ezonebot): web_backend.host=172.29.112.1 with enabled=true, router_debug_external_access(+confirmed)=true (backup config.json.bak-20260919-121239). The next launch in that workspace binds the router to the WSL-reachable address, accepts external clients with the external token, and attaches the MCP entry."
caveats:
  - "The WSL host address can change with the distribution's NAT gateway; if a launch then fails to bind, set the new address (or pass --ca-web-address <ip> for one launch)."
  - "The native-Windows Muse settings path (~/.config/muse/settings.json on Windows) is untested; the WSL path is the one this machine uses and the one verified."
  - "The running Muse session (started before this change) keeps the old setup until it is relaunched; a loopback-bound router is deliberately not attached (Muse would only show a dead server)."
state: "Working tree; committed and deployed as the pinned snapshot; the published nightly (c3a76f4) carries the restart CLI but not this attach logic."
